Third-party code and models in the decision-model runtime (engine/decision/, stage A, 2026-10-01):

- Laya SDK 0.3.4 (https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya), Copyright Convai Innovations,
  Apache License 2.0. Ported with changes, each file saying which: engine/decision/laya/sequence.py,
  head.py, encoder.py, router.py, lang.py. The license text is engine/decision/laya/LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.
  The Laya checkpoints the engine loads (convaiinnovations/laya: English, multilingual,
  typed-decisions) are Apache-2.0 and are not part of this repository.
- ModernBERT (Answer.AI), the encoder of the English and typed-decisions checkpoints, and mmBERT
  (JHU CLSP), the encoder of the multilingual one; their weights are inside the Laya checkpoints
  and run through Hugging Face transformers (Apache-2.0), a dependency, not included.
- The request and response shape of /v1/systemone is TypeSafe AI's Jev System One contract (the
  `state`, `model` and `questions` contract with the choice, score and noul question types); this
  is a compatible implementation, not an affiliated or endorsed one.
- arbiter (https://github.com/0xBakeer/arbiter, MIT, same author): the batcher, the request
  validation, the error bodies and the equivalence tool (tools/decider_equivalence.py,
  tools/decider_cases.py) were ported from it.

Runtime dependencies of the installable package (pyproject.toml: the proxy and the dashboard),
installed by pip, none of their code copied into this repository:

- cryptography (https://github.com/pyca/cryptography), Apache License 2.0 or BSD 3-Clause, at
  the user's choice: AES-256-GCM for the backends' keys at rest (proxy/secrets.py).
- With the `host` extra: psutil (https://github.com/giampaolo/psutil), BSD 3-Clause, and
  nvidia-ml-py (NVIDIA's NVML bindings), BSD 3-Clause: the host collector (proxy/hostcollect.py).

The plugins in plugins/ (tandemllm-vllm-plugin, tandemllm-sglang-plugin) are part of TandemLLM under
the same license and have no dependencies. They run inside vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm)
and SGLang (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang), both Apache License 2.0, and import them at run
time; none of their code is copied into this repository.
